# kilix runtime settings
#
# This tracked file documents immutable defaults for Kilix-specific settings.
# Put user overrides in ~/.local/gpu_terminal/kilix/config/kilix.env. The
# launcher reads simple KEY=value lines and exports only known KILIX_* keys;
# lines are intentionally not shell-evaluated.
# Storage roots are process/service settings, not persisted here: use
# KILIX_STORAGE_HOME and KILIX95_STORAGE_HOME in the launching environment.
#
# Clickable chrome is shared by all projects in
# ~/.local/gpu_terminal/settings.conf and is managed by `kilix-settings`.
# Legacy KILIX_CHROME_CLOCK/BATTERY values here are migrated when that shared
# file is first created, but new chrome preferences belong in settings.conf.
#
# Read-aloud and dictation are shared settings as well. KILIX_CHROME_SPEAK and
# KILIX_CHROME_DICTATE show the two tab-bar widgets; the KILIX_VOICE_* keys
# configure what a click does. They exist only in settings.conf: there is no
# legacy value to migrate, so unlike the two chrome keys above they are not
# read from this file. Values are presets, and an unrecognized one reads back
# as the default:
#   KILIX_VOICE_TTS_ENGINE=espeak        espeak | mbrola | off
#   KILIX_VOICE_TTS_VOICE=en-us          synthesizer voice name
#   KILIX_VOICE_TTS_RATE=170             120 | 150 | 170 | 200 | 240 (wpm)
#   KILIX_VOICE_TTS_EXTENT=screen        screen | scrollback | selection
#   KILIX_VOICE_TTS_MAX_CHARS=4000       1000 | 4000 | 16000 | unlimited
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_ENGINE=vosk          vosk | vibevoice | off
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_MODEL=small-en-us    small-en-us | lgraph-en-us | vibevoice-asr-bitnet
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_SUBMIT=never         never | confirm
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_MAX_SECONDS=30       15 | 30 | 60 | 120
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_SILENCE_MS=900       500 | 900 | 1500
#   KILIX_VOICE_STT_PUNCTUATION=1        write spoken "period", "new line", ...
#   KILIX_VOICE_DEVICE_IN=default        PulseAudio source name, or default
#   KILIX_VOICE_DEVICE_OUT=default       PulseAudio sink name, or default
#   KILIX_VOICE_HISTORY=off              off | on, kilix-stt's dictation log
# Both widgets ship enabled, which means the buttons are visible and clickable.
# Nothing opens the microphone until one is clicked, and dictation has no
# setting that submits what it heard: it types the text and stops there.
#
# Runtime examples:
# KILIX_DESKTOP_PROVIDER=auto
# KILIX_DESKTOP_FLAVOR=xp
# KILIX_DESKTOP_PROVIDER=cap
# KILIX_CAP_DIR=/absolute/path/to/kilix-cap
# KILIX_CAP_REF=<full-40-character-commit-sha>
# KILIX_CAP_AUTO_INSTALL=1
# KILIX_DESKTOP_PROVIDER=tui
# KILIX_TUI_UTILS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/kilix-tui-utils
# KILIX_TUI_UTILS_REF=<full-40-character-commit-sha>
# KILIX_TUI_UTILS_AUTO_INSTALL=1
# KILIX_RUN_AUTO_FIT=1
# KILIX_BROWSE_BACKEND=presenter
# KILIX_HW=1
# KILIX_SHELL_INTEGRATION=0
# KILIX_PTY_BROKER=1
# KILIX_PTY_BROKER_HOME=~/.local/gpu_terminal/sources/kitty-pty-broker
# KILIX_PTY_BROKER_AUTO_RECOVER=1
# KILIX_PTY_BROKER_JOURNAL_LIMIT=67108864
# KILIX95_REF=<full-40-character-commit-sha>
# KILIX95_DIR=~/.local/gpu_terminal/sources/kilix-95
# KILIX95_ALLOW_MUTABLE_REF=0
# KILIX95_ALLOW_UNPINNED_INSTALL=0
# KILIX_REPO=https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/kilix.git
# KILIX_TRUST_EXISTING_CHECKOUT=0
# KILIX_ALLOW_MUTABLE_REF=0
# KILIX_PREBUILT_VERSION=0.47.0
# KILIX_PREBUILT_SHA256=<sha256>
# KILIX_ALLOW_UNVERIFIED_PREBUILT=0
# KILIX_BUILD_MODE=system
# KILIX_KITTY_DEPS_URL=<immutable-versioned-asset-url>
# KILIX_KITTY_DEPS_SHA256=<sha256>
# KILIX_NERD_FONT_URL=<versioned-asset-url>
# KILIX_NERD_FONT_SHA256=<sha256>
# KILIX_NERD_FONT_FILE_SHA256=<sha256>

# Pinned Tmux Manager download-on-first-run closure. The launcher supplies
# immutable defaults; uncomment only to point at another reviewed closure.
# TMUX_TUI_REPO=https://github.com/itsmygithubacct/tmux-tui.git
# TMUX_TUI_REF=<full-40-character-commit-sha>
# TMUX_CLI_REF=<full-40-character-commit-sha>
# Prefix overrides must be normalized absolute paths.
# TMUX_TUI_PREFIX=$HOME/.local
# KILIX_GO_TOOLCHAIN=go1.26.5
# KILIX_PYTHON=/path/to/python3.12
